  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improved capacity of the government and social partners to deliver skills development training</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building on the ILO Programme of Support for Syria, the ILO is strengthening the capacity of the government and social partners to deliver inclusive skills development training, with a focus on TVET, skills profiling, skills gap analysis, and demand-driven learning pathways. The intervention supports better alignment between labour market needs and training provision through evidence-based planning, coordination with UN and national counterparts, and practical measures to improve employability, enterprise recovery, and access to decent work for women, youth, returnees, and other vulnerable groups. It also promotes stronger linkages between training institutions, employers, and workers&#x2019; organizations to support a more responsive and resilient skills system.</narrative>
  </description>
